        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Channel Coding - Capacity and Error-Correcting Codes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nNOISY CHANNEL CODING THEOREM (Shannon, 1948):\n  For any channel with capacity C bits/use:\n  • If R < C: ∃ a code such that P_e → 0 as block length n → ∞\n  • If R > C: P_e → 1 for all codes (unavoidable error)"
    },
