        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Channel Coding - Capacity and Error-Correcting Codes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PRACTICAL CODES vs SHANNON LIMIT:\n  1950: Hamming codes — first error-correcting, far from capacity\n  1960: Reed-Solomon — algebraic, excellent burst error correction (CDs, QR codes)\n  1993: Turbo codes — within 0.5 dB of Shannon limit (3GPP LTE data)\n  1997: LDPC rediscovered — within 0.01 dB (5G NR data channels)\n  2009: Polar codes — provably capacity-achieving, O(n log n) complexity (5G NR control)\n```"
